       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this one, even with your confirmation. 50 mg of amlodipine is five times the maximum dose. I know of no indication for it in a 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function. At that dose I'd expect severe, prolonged hypotension and possibly shock that doesn't respond well to treatment. I don't want to put an order into the system that could seriously harm the patient when there's no rationale I can document.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** I can order 10 mg by mouth once daily, or 5 mg if you want to titrate. I'll enter either one as soon as you say so.\n- **Enter it through pharmacy.** If there's a specific reason for this dose that I don't know about, call the pharmacist and have them enter or co-sign it directly. They can document the rationale and set up monitoring.\n- **Check for a mix-up.** The intended dose may have been 5 mg, or the order may have been meant for a different drug.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
